Category: IT Services Location: GoPro Consultancy is urgently looking for a (Senior) IT Recruiter to enlarge the recruitment team in Colombo. As an IT Recruitment Specialist, you will be responsible for identifying candidates to suit our needs by using different platforms to conduct thorough research. Work closely with Project Managers to ensure the quality of our candidates. 
 Candidates need to be fluent in English. 
 Tasks and Responsibilities 
 Search and match qualified candidates, through company database, professional media channels, job boards, and other resources; 
 Determine applicant qualifications by interviewing applicants; 
 analyzing responses, verify references, and compare qualifications to job requirements; 
 Maintain effective relationships with professional networks to source qualified candidates; 
 Cold call candidates to gauge their interest in current and future job opportunities; 
 Ensure the company’s database of candidate records are up-to-date and administer them to complete these records; 
 Follow up with new and existing candidates and keep them apprised of our latest opportunities; 
 Profile 
 ​ 
 +1 year of recruitment experience;Experience with technical or IT recruiting is an advantage; 
 Experience with LinkedIn recruiter is an advantage; 
 Target drivenFull proficiency in English; 
 Out-going personality; 
 Excellent computer skills; 
 Attention to detail; 
 Experience in working to and exceeding targets; 
 Comfortable in conducting one-on-o

Please submit your resume in English and indicate your level of English proficiency. Mindrift connects specialists with project-based AI opportunities for leading tech companies, focused on testing, evaluating, and improving AI systems. Participation is project-based, not permanent employment. What this opportunity involves Annotation is what helps AI make sense of the world. As an annotator, you may be invited to take part in online projects such as rating AI-generated content, evaluating factual accuracy, or comparing responses — when projects are available. While each project involves unique tasks, contributors may: 
 Carefully review provided data (text, images, or videos); 
 Label or classify content based on project guidelines; 
 Identify and flag factually incorrect, sensitive, inappropriate, or unclear material. 
 What we look for This opportunity is a good fit for candidates open to part-time, non-permanent projects. Ideally, contributors will have: 
 Bachelor’s degree in any discipline; 
 Minimum 1 year of experience in any professional role; 
 Logical thinking, fact-checking and reasoning abilities; 
 Strong attention to detail and ability to understand and follow complex instructions; 
 Strong communication skills, including the ability to ask clarifying questions when needed; 
 Genuine interest in technology and artificial intelligence; 
 Strong written and spoken English (C1+). 
